From 3266f2b5ddb754324a8f986e932af6209ca9a05f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MatthieuPe <matthieupelissier01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:46:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Docs: the two DES 2018 tests explained; talk figures of the
 DES sky

- project_overview: the line model is one network trained end to end on
  the line loss; why a U-Net before the line sums and a CNN over them;
  the known-track and blind tests and why they give 11 and 8 of 14;
  the real DES CMD and Figure 4 in sections 2 and 3
- overview figures: two-test scorecard replaces the mixed one
- summary: one paragraph on 11 versus 8
- line_model/run.py: des2018_excess_maps factored out of des2018_gif;
  talk_figures (step talk-figures) writes talk_des_sky.png and
  talk_des_sky_found.png (line network's lines along the DES 2018 tracks)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012RPeQZf5ApmdhrmSymBM4S
